        kind: 'worked',
        text: 'Feeders A and B form a ring and can each carry 300 A. A peaks at 190 A, B at 150 A. A fault close to the substation leaves all of feeder A without supply.\n\nAll of A onto B: 190 + 150 = 340 A, 113% of 300 A: too much. Half of A onto B, about 95 A: 150 + 95 = 245 A, 82%: that works. The other half waits for the repair, or goes via a third link. So the reserve is only partial.\n\nFor full reserve the sum must stay below 300 A: it is 40 A too much. Moving the open point doesn’t help, because the sum stays the same. Options: a link to a feeder from a neighbouring station, or a new feeder that takes over part of A.',
